            <ArticleTitle>Central Pain Following Cord Severance for Cephalosomatic Anastomosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/cns.12527</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One of the key obstacles to a successful head transplant is the possible onset of central pain, a chronic pain condition that would impair the quality of life of the transplantee. In this review, we provide the reader with a knowledge of this neglected aspect of the head transplant initiative and outline the management should this eventuality occur.</AbstractText>
